WEBVTT
Language: en

NOTE
Voiced by Tello (AI voice). Timings match the voiced cut of the video.

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:11.205
A new Lite account — facility and staff compliance only. No MAR, no 602A, no PHI.

00:00:11.555 --> 00:00:16.498
Walkthrough offers both: take the tour on screen, or read the same seven screens.

00:00:16.848 --> 00:00:26.911
Step 1 of 7 — Your trainers and their codes. One row per trainer: their link, how many signed up through it, how many of those are paying, and the commission rate on record.

00:00:27.261 --> 00:00:35.639
Step 2 — A code is a longer trial. Somebody arriving on a trainer's link gets the trial length set on that code instead of the default.

00:00:35.989 --> 00:00:44.943
Step 3 — This is the number that matters. Requirements that are current, out of requirements that exist. Here, 7 of 119.

00:00:45.293 --> 00:00:54.887
Step 4 — And it tells you whose. Six overdue, 55 due this month. An expired TB test is a named person, not a red number on a chart.

00:00:55.237 --> 00:01:02.933
Step 5 — The checklist an analyst works from. Title 22 requirements with dates against them, overdue at the top.

00:01:03.283 --> 00:01:08.333
Step 6 — Now ask me something. Tello answers from this facility's own records.

00:01:08.683 --> 00:01:15.738
Step 7 — Everything else is in here. Documents, the audit log, billing. Walkthrough replays this tour any time.

00:01:16.088 --> 00:01:20.498
Back on the dashboard: overdue items with their dates, then the quick actions.

00:01:22.988 --> 00:01:30.342
The menu — staff, in-service, training, lessons, team access, checklist, documents, Tello, audit log, billing, partners.

00:01:31.228 --> 00:01:35.659
Documents. Upload a file, tag what it is, and it is stored privately.

00:01:38.038 --> 00:01:46.075
Billing — the current plan, then Lite at $29, Multi-Home at $79, and Agency as Contact Sales.
